{
  "title": "Prepositions and places in town",
  "note": "Each preposition takes a fixed case. With the ablative: a/ab, cum, de, e/ex, pro, sine. With the accusative: ad, ante, apud, circum, contra, inter, per, post, prope, propter, trans. In and sub take the accusative for motion into or under and the ablative for position: in urbem, into the city; in urbe, in the city.",
